;; seed/tests/kir/doclib/doclib.kotoba -- SOURCE of the KIR document library that seed/12-kirread.kotoba embeds (agent KIR4,
;; 2026-10-03). gen-doclib.py turns the defns below (comments and blank lines dropped, one defn per line) into the string
;; functions kr-doc-text* of 12-kirread; `gen-doclib.py --check` fails when the two differ.
;;
;; Representation: a KIR :document is a :string holding its CANONICAL EDN text, exactly as stage-0's native backend
;; (kotoba-lang/kotoba-native src/kotoba/native/document.cljk, "gap 2 of the selfhost foundation"): nil, true/false, a
;; decimal i64, an escaped string, a keyword's text, [a b] (a b) #{a b} {k v k v} with one space between forms, set items
;; and map keys in canonical order. Every helper is a port of the kotoba$doc-* helper of the same meaning (same scans, same
;; order, same bounds: 32 items, depth 8 + 1, 4096 nodes; the same traps, through an out-of-range vector read). The
;; differences are the seed's spelling only: string-find-byte and string-append-range are written out (no loader call),
;; region-compare takes 5 parameters (its end is always the key's length), (bool-not x) is (not x).
;; Entry points (12-kirread respells the KIR head to these): __kr_dnull __kr_dbool __kr_di64 __kr_desc __kr_dsym
;; __kr_dcount __kr_dkind __kr_deq __kr_dsetc __kr_dcontains __kr_dget __kr_dvat __kr_dlat __kr_dentry __kr_dvassoc
;; __kr_dconj __kr_dvdrop __kr_dvremove __kr_dvsort __kr_dassocop __kr_ddissocop __kr_dmerge __kr_dstrval __kr_dboolval
;; __kr_di64val __kr_did; the folds of document-vector/list/set/map use __kr_dvz __kr_dlz __kr_dsz __kr_dmz (empty),
;; __kr_dvadd __kr_dsetput __kr_dmapputu (one step) and __kr_dbounded (the whole).
